\n   - Total: 7 winning tiles\\n\\nPlaying T9 gives me the most flexible waiting pattern with the highest number of available winning tiles (T3 and T4).\\n\\nReason: \\nDiscarding T9 maximizes my winning opportunities. After discarding T9, I'll be waiting on T3 or T4, giving me 3+3=6 potential winning tiles remaining. This is superior to other options. With T3, I complete the chow [T2,T3,T4] and can pair with T4,T9. With T4, I form a pung [T4,T4,T4] and need to win on T3 to complete [T2,T3,T4] pattern or adjust for pair.\\n\\nAnswer: Play T9\"}"}
